+composeFixedWidthRows, so user/queued bubbles receive semantic suffix
+recomposition and width-run-local bubble sizing rather than canonical
+whole-message geometry.
|
|- Finding 2 — improved but not fully resolved. Cached cursor ranges
+remove the full group-boundary scans and repeated
+userMessageTextRowOffsets work. However, every composeSemanticUserRows
+call invokes renderAdaptiveUserMessageRows(owner.text, ...), which
+still:
|- runs sanitizeUntrustedText over the complete owner text, and
|- splits the complete text into hard lines.
|
|A long user message can therefore still cost O(whole message length)
+during probe, narrow recomposition, and full-tail recomposition, even
+when only O(H) source rows are needed. This is a medium performance
+issue relative to the strict viewport-height goal. Caching sanitized
+hard lines or passing a cached flow document/range into the adaptive
+renderer would complete the fix.
|
|I found no new high/medium correctness bug in the current diff.
