=== 1784499348103-9orxqs#12 (gpt-5.6-sol)
|This is primarily our rendering/parsing issue, not poor mathematical
+notation from the AI.
|
|The AI returned valid, reasonably structured LaTeX:
|
|▎ latex
|▎ \\[
|▎ \\forall x\\exists y\\Big(
|▎ (y\\times y\\times y=x)
|▎ \\land
|▎ \\forall z\\big(
|▎ (z\\times z\\times z=x)\\Rightarrow(z=y)
|▎ \\big)
|▎ \\Big).
|▎ \\]
|
|In a normal KaTeX/MathJax renderer, those source newlines are treated as
+ordinary whitespace. It would appear as one coherent equation with
+properly sized parentheses.
|
|Our terminal renderer currently:
|
|1. preserves every physical newline inside display math;
|2. removes layout commands such as \\Big and \\big;
|3. renders each remaining source line separately.
|
|That leaves isolated operators and parentheses, producing the awkward
+result you noticed.
|
|The correct fix is to collapse source newlines into spaces for
+ordinary display equations, then let Exocortex wrap the resulting
+expression naturally to the available width. We should preserve explicit
+line structure only inside environments such as aligned, matrix, and
+cases.
|
|That would make this render approximately as:
|
|▎ text
