|## Local-main merge
|
|Merged local main into math-rendering
+successfully.
|
|- Merge commit: b98625e
|- Local main: 523d624
|- Conflicts: None
|- Worktree status: Clean
|- Merged into main: No — stopped as
+requested
|- Worktree daemon and xenv are stopped.
|
|## Validation
|
|- TUI suite: 635 passed, 0 failed
|- Post-merge xenv + exotest showcase
+check passed
|- git diff --check: clean
|- Full repository suite: 1,368 passed, 1
+unrelated failure
|- The failure is the environment-sensitive
+DeepSeek authentication test detecting
+shared credentials.
|- Typecheck still reports four pre-existing
+narrowing errors in historycursor.test.ts;
+the same errors occur on local main.
|
|## Code assessment
|
|### Merge blocker: currency corruption
|
|The dollar-delimiter heuristic can
+misinterpret common currency ranges as math
+and remove their dollar signs:
|
|▎ text
|▎ Range: $5-$10.            → Range: 5-10.
|▎ Basic ($5) / Pro ($10)    → Basic (5) / Pr
+▎ o (10)
|
|This changes the meaning of rendered and
+copied text, so I recommend fixing it before
+merging.
|
|### Other issues worth addressing
|
|1. Dollar spans may cross hard newlines
|- Physical newlines are temporarily replaced
+with private-use separators for multiline
+Markdown parsing.
|- The dollar parser can consequently pair
+dollar signs from separate lines, even
+though $...$ should remain single-line.
|
|2. Display math immediately following
+prose
|- Without a blank line before \\[, paragraph
+collection can absorb the display block and
+render it as inline math.
|- The paragraph collector should stop when
+the next physical line begins a display-math
+block.
|
|3. Quadratic malformed-input scanning
|- Repeated unclosed \\( delimiters cause
+repeated scans to the end of the input.
|- Large malformed or streaming content could
+temporarily freeze the synchronous renderer.
|
|4. Raw table/matrix delimiter splitting
|- Literal | inside table-cell math can be
+mistaken for a Markdown column separator.
|- Escaped \\& inside matrix text can be
+mistaken for a matrix cell separator.
|- Matrix columns with unequal widths are not
+padded/aligned.
|
|5. Malformed TeX fallback is lossy
|- The dependency often tolerates malformed
+input rather than throwing, so our catch
+fallback does not activate.
|- Unknown-command braces can be silently
+removed instead of preserving the original
+expression.
|
|6. Very narrow rendering edge case
|- At a one-column width, a width-two
+supplementary Unicode character such as an
+emoji can be split into invalid UTF-16
+surrogate rows.
|
|### Dependency assessment
|
|@devhub-io/latex-to-unicode@2.0.1 is:
|
|- exact-version pinned;
|- MIT-licensed;
|- small;
|- dependency-free;
|- free of install scripts.
|
|However, it is only several days old, has a
+very small maintenance footprint, and this
+repository intentionally tracks no
+lockfile/integrity record. That creates a
+moderate maintenance and supply-chain risk.
|
|## Strengths
|
|- The showcased logical notation now renders
+clearly.
|- Display math is white and left-aligned as
+requested.
|- Pretty-printed ordinary display math is
+collapsed correctly.
|- Matrices, cases, and aligned environments
+retain intentional rows.
|- Inline and fenced code protection is
+well-covered.
|- Common symbols, quantifiers, scripts,
+roots, fractions, and Greek letters work.
|- Terminal-width measurement and
+display-math copy projections are integrated
+correctly.
|- Rendering errors are contained rather than
+crashing the conversation.
|
|## Recommendation
|
|Not ready to merge into main yet. The
+currency corruption is a definite blocker. I
+would also fix multiline dollar pairing,
+display-block boundaries, and
+malformed-input performance before
+requesting final merge approval.
