|▎ typescript
|▎ case "after": newCursor = Math.min(cursor 
+▎ + 1, buffer.length); break;
|
|When the cursor is at the last character of
+a line (the character just before \\n),
+pressing "a" moves the cursor to cursor +
+1, which lands on the \\n itself. In insert
+mode, that could mean the cursor ends up at
+the start of the next line visually,
+crossing the line boundary. The fix should
+clamp to lineEndOf(buffer, cursor) — which
+returns the position of the \\n (or
+buffer.length). That's valid for insert mode
+(you can insert at the end of the line,
+right before the \\n).
|
|Wait, let me think again. lineEndOf returns
+the index of the \\n character. So if cursor
+is at position pos which is the last char
+before \\n, then cursor + 1 = position of
+\\n. And lineEndOf(buffer, cursor) also
+returns the position of \\n. So those would
+be equal.
|
|The problem must be when the cursor IS on
+the \\n character in normal mode (possible?
+Let me check clampNormal). Actually, in
+normal mode the clampNormal prevents the
