=== 1776395204803-9oas53#excerpt (gpt-5.4)
|                              ⎛ QKᵀ ⎞
+  Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax⎜ ─── ⎟V
+                              ⎝ √dₖ ⎠
|
|A masked version adds a mask M before
+softmax to block forbidden positions, which
+is essential for autoregressive decoding:
|
|         ⎛ QKᵀ     ⎞
+  softmax⎜ ─── + M ⎟V
+         ⎝ √dₖ     ⎠
|
|                              ⎛ QKᵀ ⎞
+  Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax⎜ ─── ⎟V
+                              ⎝ √dₖ ⎠
|
|- The dot products QKᵀ give relevance
+scores.
|- The √dₖ scaling keeps scores from becoming
+too sharp.
|- The output is a weighted sum of values;
+each output row lies in the convex hull of
+the value vectors.
|
|    MultiHead(Q, K, V)
+      = Concat(head₁, …, headₕ)Wᴼ
|    headᵢ = Attention(QWᵢ^Q, KWᵢᴷ, VWᵢⱽ)
|
|- Masked / causal attention: used in
+autoregressive decoders so a position cannot
+attend to future tokens. This is implemented
+by adding −∞ above the diagonal before
+softmax.
|- The page also mentions older or
+alternative forms such as
+Bahdanau/additive attention,
+Luong/multiplicative attention,
+positional variants, and spatial/channel
+attention in CNNs.
|
|### Computational tradeoffs
|The big cost is that the attention matrix is
+quadratic in sequence length (O(n²)
+memory and compute), which becomes expensive
+for long contexts. The page highlights two
+optimizations:
|- FlashAttention: computes attention in
+blocks to reduce GPU memory use while
+preserving exact results.
|- FlexAttention: a PyTorch/Meta kernel that
+allows score modification before softmax and
+selects efficient implementations
+dynamically."
`;
